1. Date range
The Netflix data covers January 2023 through June 2026, across 7 six-month reporting periods.
2. Number of titles
The dataset contains 24,427 unique titles.
3. Bridgerton
The Bridgerton universe, including spin-offs, generated 4,862,800,000 viewing hours.
4. Stranger Things
The five main seasons of Stranger Things generated 5,548,500,000 viewing hours.
5. Top 10 titles
In the first half of 2026, the top 10 individual titles accounted for 6.1% of viewing hours. “Other Shows” was excluded because it represents a grouped category, not an individual title.
6. Global availability
Globally available titles represented 24.60% of unique titles and accounted for 51.92% of total viewing hours.

Supporting Calculations for the Memo


Show code
global_by_period &lt;- NETFLIX_DATA |&gt;
  summarise(share = sum(hours_viewed[available_globally %in% TRUE]) / sum(hours_viewed),
            .by = period)

global_share_first &lt;- global_by_period |&gt; filter(period == "2023H1") |&gt; pull(share)
global_share_last  &lt;- global_by_period |&gt; filter(period == "2026H1") |&gt; pull(share)

top_title_max_share &lt;- NETFLIX_DATA |&gt;
  summarise(hours = sum(hours_viewed), .by = c(period, title)) |&gt;
  mutate(share = hours / sum(hours), .by = period) |&gt;
  filter_out(str_detect(title, "^Other (Shows|Films|Movies)$")) |&gt;
  slice_max(share, n = 1, by = period) |&gt;
  summarise(max_share = max(share)) |&gt;
  pull(max_share)

global_by_period |&gt;
  gt() |&gt;
  tab_header(title = "Share of Hours from Globally Available Titles") |&gt;
  fmt_percent(share, decimals = 1) |&gt;
  cols_label(period = "Reporting Period", share = "Share of Hours")








